From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: prefer a device-specific regdb.bin

ath12k loads the regulatory database from board-2.bin before trying a
standalone regdb.bin. Where the platform provisions the vendor regulatory
database the OEM firmware loads (the Cambium X7-35X stages its own
regdb.bin from the unit's OEM firmware at boot), that file must win over
the generic database in board-2.bin.

Try regdb.bin first; fall back to board-2.bin when it is absent.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -580,6 +580,16 @@
 {
 	char boardname[BOARD_NAME_SIZE], default_boardname[BOARD_NAME_SIZE];
 	int ret;
+
+	/* A device-specific regdb.bin provisioned next to the firmware (e.g.
+	 * the vendor regulatory database the OEM loads) takes precedence over
+	 * the generic regdb carried in board-2.bin.
+	 */
+	ret = ath12k_core_fetch_board_data_api_1(ab, bd, ATH12K_REGDB_FILE_NAME);
+	if (!ret) {
+		ath12k_info(ab, "using device-specific %s\n", ATH12K_REGDB_FILE_NAME);
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	ret = ath12k_core_create_board_name(ab, boardname, BOARD_NAME_SIZE);
 	if (ret) {
